      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boonville%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1836 Hain House and Memorial Garden, built in 1830s style, stands as one of Boonville’s oldest landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://boonvillemo.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kemper Military School, the oldest military academy west of the Mississippi, operated in Boonville from 1844 to 2002.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://boonvillemo.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cooper County Jail, erected in 1848, served as Missouri’s longest‑serving jail until it closed in 1979.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boonville%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Boonville endured two battles and two occupations, making it a key north‑south and east‑west crossroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://boonvillemo.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 1911‑12 Katy Depot is the only surviving Spanish Mission style station on the Missouri‑Kansas‑Texas Railroad and is listed on the National Register.",
